+  <h2 id="worth-your-time">Worth your time</h2>
+
+  <div class="sl-picks">
+    <div class="sl-pick">
+      <p class="sl-pick-num">01 &middot; Listen</p>
+      <h3 class="sl-pick-title">A New Way to Think About Your Time</h3>
+      <p>10% Happier with Dan Harris, with Harvard Business School professor Ashley Whillans. Why so many working adults feel time poor at every income level, what she calls "time confetti," and the time audit this week's worksheet is built on.</p>
+      <a class="sl-pick-link" href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/id1087147821?i=1000536756404" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Listen to the episode</a>
+    </div>
+    <div class="sl-pick">
+      <p class="sl-pick-num">02 &middot; Read</p>
+      <h3 class="sl-pick-title">Want to Be Happier? Spend Some Money on Avoiding Household Chores</h3>
+      <p>Harvard Business School Working Knowledge, on a study of more than 6,000 people. Those who paid to hand off tasks they disliked reported greater life satisfaction. Yet only 2 percent of working adults in one group said they would spend an extra $40 that way.</p>
+      <p><strong>My take:</strong> What's the value of your time? Whether it is an opportunity to make more money with that same amount of time with work or a side gig, or the non-monetary value of having that time for you and your family…</p>
+      <a class="sl-pick-link" href="https://www.library.hbs.edu/working-knowledge/want-to-be-happier-spend-some-money-on-avoiding-household-chores" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the article</a>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+
+  <p><strong>P.S. </strong>Tell me the hour you claimed. The day, the time and what it is for. Saying it out loud is half of keeping it.</p>
