   <p>Name the cause first: the load, the people, the story, the fit, or something bigger. Then pick the fix that matches. If your mood is low most days, start with your doctor or a therapist.</p>
   <h3>Can you be happy at a job you don't love?</h3>
   <p>Yes. Many happy people have jobs they like well enough, with clear edges, decent people, and plenty of room for the life outside it. Loving the job is a bonus, not a requirement.</p>
