   <p>If your days off are for recovery, if you feel guilty resting, or if the people closest to you get the tired version of you, you are working more than your life can absorb.</p>
   <h3>How do I stop letting work ruin my life?</h3>
   <p>Start with one boundary, such as a shutdown time or one protected evening. Keep it for two weeks. Small, consistent changes beat a big plan you abandon.</p>
